// The http-facing /compile request (reducer-targets B10c; operator artifact-list design via v-hivemind): the
// body a client POSTs to the /compile route — the COMPLETE kinded-artifact list the client assembled, mirroring
// rcdzc::compile's own &[Artifact] (kind + name + bytes). Value.encode/Value.decode'd as the request body
// (canonical binary-AST — the exchange format, operator standing directive; NOT JSON).
//
// Each artifact's payload is EITHER Inline (bytes carried in the request) OR CasRef (a 33-byte ProgramHash the
// handler blobs.gets). So a big AST rides by-reference (kind="ast", CasRef(astHash from /parse)) while a tiny
// name rides inline (kind="entry", Inline(encode_name(entry-file-name))). The handler resolves every payload to
// bytes and hands rcdzc the SAME bytes-only Artifact(kind,name,bytes) list it already takes — no per-kind
// special-casing, no entry synthesis. Any future kind (spans → wasm-debug/dwarf, result-types, …) just goes in
// the list; small ones Inline, big ones CasRef; the handler + rcdzc are unchanged.
//
// INVARIANT (operator): the CAS lives ONLY here (the handler's domain). Payload/Inline/CasRef must NOT appear in
// rcdzc's CompileRequest/Artifact wire — rcdzc stays bytes-only + CAS-agnostic (the compiler knows nothing about
// the CAS). Named RouteArtifact (not Artifact) so this co-imports cleanly with rcdzc-compile's Artifact.
type Payload       = | Inline(Bytes) | CasRef(Bytes)
type RouteArtifact = | RouteArtifact(Record(kind: String, name: String, payload: Payload))
type CompileRoute  = | Compile(Record(artifacts: List(RouteArtifact)))

export { Payload.*, RouteArtifact.*, CompileRoute.* }
